  "body": "## What changed\n\nReported on Windows 10 and Fedora: \"shortcut icons in the toolbar are missing\". On a fresh install nobody has pinned an operation, so the ribbon's whole Create run is the section dropdown doors (Milling 2D…, Milling 3D…, Drilling…, Multi-axis…) plus the machine door (Milling…) - and `icon_of` returned no glyph for `Cmd::More` and `Cmd::Machine` by design, so that whole stretch read as text-only between fully-iconed groups.\n\n- `icon_of` (crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs) now takes `&State` and gives:\n  - section doors their family's op glyph: Milling 2D → pocket, Milling 3D → 3D finish, Drilling → drill, Multi-axis → multi-axis rough, Turning → face;\n  - the machine door its workspace's: Milling → face mill, Turning → turned bar (rotary contour), Mill-turning → rotary parallel.\n- All from the existing icon set - no new asset. The View door stays caption-only (a layout list).\n- Snapshots `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png` move by those glyphs. **They overlap PR #188 and PR #201's snapshot changes** - whichever merges later regenerates them.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#207).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: every binary green (lib 240 passed, 2 ignored). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::ribbon_icon_tests::every_ribbon_cell_of_every_workspace_wears_a_glyph` - Milling, Turning and Mill-turning with no pins: every cell but View has a glyph (on main the section doors and machine door fail it).\n- `egui_app::ribbon_icon_tests::the_machine_door_wears_its_workspace`\n\nChangelog: Ribbon section and machine doors show icons (the Create run was text-only with no pinned operations)\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #207\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
